---
import DashboardLayout from '../../layouts/DashboardLayout.astro';
import TopUpForm from '../../islands/wallet/TopUpForm.astro';
// The three figures in this paragraph are config values, read through the same module
// the landing page uses. They were HARDCODED here, which made this the third and fourth
// place the two minimums were written out: consolidating the landing page's two copies
// into one constant did not touch this file, and no guard could see it, because
// tests/prices.test.ts checks the CONSTANT against config/apikita.toml and the constant
// was right. The two copies here were invisible to it by construction.
//
// That is the failure this file is now evidence of: a fix that consolidates SOME copies
// of a value, and a check that pins the consolidated one.
import { minFirstDepositIdr, minTopupIdr, topupPerHour, idr } from '../../lib/models.ts';

//
// THE PARAGRAPH BELOW IS ONE LINE ON PURPOSE. A line break on either side of an
// {expression} is collapsed by Astro, so the space lands on whichever side is NOT the
// break: the page first rendered "at least10,000 IDR", and after moving the break it
// rendered "10,000IDR". Neither was visible in the source and both were on the page a
// customer reads before their first payment. Read the BUILT page, not the template.
//
// REMOVED: `const topupPerHour = 5;` sat on this line and SHADOWED the import above.
// The page published the local literal, and tests/prices.test.ts - which compares the
// imported constant against config/apikita.toml - stayed green while checking a value
// this page never rendered. Changing that line to 7 changed the built HTML to
// "rate-limited to 7 per hour" with every test still passing.
//
// It is the failure the comment above describes, committed by the very edit that
// describes it: the two minimums were consolidated into one constant and the rate cap
// was left behind as a second copy. The declaration is DELETED rather than corrected -
// a second copy that happens to agree today is still a second copy, and no test can
// keep two copies agreeing. What renders now is the imported constant.
---

<DashboardLayout title="Wallet">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Wallet</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm text-ink-muted">
    Prepaid balance, topped up by QRIS through Midtrans. Minimums differ: your first deposit is at least {idr(minFirstDepositIdr)} IDR, and later top-ups at least {idr(minTopupIdr)} IDR. Top-up creation is rate-limited to {topupPerHour} per hour.
</p>


  <div class="mt-8">
    <TopUpForm />
  </div>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-2xl rounded-lg border border-edge bg-surface-raised p-4 text-sm text-ink-muted">
    <h2 class="font-medium text-ink">How crediting works</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Midtrans notifies our server directly, the server verifies the notification's
      signature and matches it against the stored order, and only then does the
      balance move — in one transaction. The browser is never trusted to say a
      payment happened, which is why a successful payment shows as
      <strong>pending</strong> here until the confirmation lands.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Balances are prepaid and non-refundable. Credit expires 2 years after each deposit. If a payment is
      confirmed and the service cannot be delivered, contact support with the order
      id above.
    </p>
  </section>
</DashboardLayout>
